| Year | Experience | Goal |
|---|---|---|
| Year 1 | Meet with an academic advisor and explore nuclear engineering organizations at UT | Successfully plan my transition into Nuclear Engineering and learn more about the field |
| Year 2 | Apply for nuclear engineering internships, research positions, or co-op opportunities | Gain practical experience and determine which area of nuclear engineering interests me most |
| Year 3 | Complete an internship, co-op, or undergraduate research experience with a nuclear-related organization | Apply engineering knowledge in a real environment and build professional connections |
| Year 4 | Complete senior nuclear engineering design work and begin applying for nuclear engineering or nuclear safety positions | Transition from college into a professional nuclear engineering career |

Possible organizations and employers I would be interested in gaining experience with include Oak Ridge National Laboratory, Y-12 National Security Complex, nuclear energy companies, and other nuclear engineering organizations in the Knoxville and Oak Ridge area.

