## Step 6 — Reflect

The only tricky part about completing the plan was how I am currently studying cybersecurity but am planning to switch to nuclear engineering. Fortunately working towards the plan helped me to get a better idea of how changing majors can affect the order of my classes as well as the amount of time I need to complete my degree. I am not exactly certain how credit transfers are going to work if I switch from one major to another so that is probably my biggest uncertainty. The four year plan connects to my POV statement because I want an education that gives me practical skills and prepares me for a real career. My SMART goals also focus on staying organized and gaining experience that will help me after college. The main thing I want to discuss with my academic advisor is how my current credits will apply to the nuclear engineering degree and how the switch will affect my graduation timeline. I also want to talk to her a little bit about which electives would be most useful or at least relevant if I want to keep cybersecurity as a secondary skill. I have a much better idea now of what I need to think about and accomplish while still leaving room to adjust as I learn more about nuclear engineering.
